## T011: generated swagger vs specs/002-us-tags-backend/contracts/openapi.yaml

Run 1 (code as left by phase-01):
- listTasks `tag` query param: in query, required false, schema string, description as contract. MATCH
- addTaskTags: POST /api/tasks/{id}/tags, id path int64 required, body $ref TaskTags required,
  200 -> Task, summary as contract. MATCH
- removeTaskTag: DELETE /api/tasks/{id}/tags, id path int64, `tag` query required string minLength 1,
  200 -> Task. MATCH
- Task.required contains `tags`; Task.tags type array of string. MATCH (the checked shape)
- DIFF-1 TaskTags.tags: extra `maxItems: 2147483647` (default max of @Size(min = 1)); contract has none.
- DIFF-2 Task.tags: missing `maxItems: 10`, `uniqueItems: true`, items `minLength: 1` / `maxLength: 30`;
  description lacks "(Q1)".

Fixes (annotations only, backend/src/main/java/com/quickflow/web/task/):
- TaskResponse.tags: @Schema -> @ArraySchema(arraySchema = @Schema(requiredMode = REQUIRED,
  description = "Lower case (Q1), ..."), maxItems = 10, uniqueItems = true,
  schema = @Schema(minLength = 1, maxLength = 30)). Run 2 output:
  "tags":{"type":"array","description":"Lower case (Q1), alphabetical; empty when the task has no tags",
  "items":{"type":"string","maxLength":30,"minLength":1},"maxItems":10,"uniqueItems":true}; `tags` still
  in Task.required. DIFF-2 fixed.
- TaskTagsRequest.tags: first tried @ArraySchema(minItems = 1) next to @NotNull @Size(min = 1): run 2
  still emitted maxItems 2147483647 (springdoc applies @Size). Replaced @NotNull @Size(min = 1) with
  @NotEmpty (same accept/reject outcome: null or empty list -> 400, field `tags`; only the default
  message text changes, which no test or spec asserts). Run 3 output:
  "TaskTags":{"type":"object","properties":{"tags":{"type":"array","description":"Each tag is trimmed
  first, then must be 1-30 characters (BR-T1); checked by the server, error field `tags`",
  "items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1}},"required":["tags"]}. DIFF-1 fixed.

Differences listed, not fixed (springdoc presentation, same as the 001 feature's D-1..D-5):
- no 400/404 responses on the operations (springdoc adds none from ApiExceptionHandler);
- 200 response description "OK" instead of the contract's prose;
- servers url http://localhost:18080 (openapi profile) vs http://localhost:8080;
- TaskTags `examples` not emitted.

Copied backend/target/openapi.json (run 3) to loops/backend-dev/outputs/openapi.json (cmp: identical).

